From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: msgbuf: send the flowring delete without waiting for tx status

brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring() waits up to 100 ms for the tx status of
the packets posted to the ring before it sends the delete request, and
clears the outstanding counter when the wait times out. The BCM4377
firmware of the MacBookAir9,1 returns the status of those packets only
for the delete request. On every disconnect, and so on every suspend,
the wait runs out:

  brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring: timed out waiting for txstatus

The status then arrives 0.5 ms after the delete request, before the
delete response, and takes the cleared counter below zero. Nothing
resets it, so the next delete of the same ring waits again. A flush
request before the wait is acknowledged by this firmware but returns no
status either.

The race the wait was added for in commit 0fa24196e425 ("wifi: brcmfmac:
fix continuous 802.1x tx pending timeout error"), txflow posting to a
ring that is being removed, is prevented by RING_CLOSING since commit
09be7546a602 ("wifi: brcmfmac: fix scheduling while atomic issue when
deleting flowring"). Tx status that arrives after the ring is removed
still releases the packet and the pending 802.1x count.

Send the delete request right away, reset the outstanding counter when
the ring is created and log a ring that is deleted with status still
outstanding.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -73,7 +73,6 @@
 #define BRCMF_MSGBUF_TRICKLE_TXWORKER_THRS	32
 #define BRCMF_MSGBUF_UPDATE_RX_PTR_THRS		48
 
-#define BRCMF_MAX_TXSTATUS_WAIT_RETRIES		10
 
 struct msgbuf_common_hdr {
 	u8				msgtype;
@@ -622,6 +621,7 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_flowring_create_worker(struct brcmf_msgbuf *msgbuf,
 	brcmf_commonring_config(msgbuf->flowrings[flowid],
 				BRCMF_H2D_TXFLOWRING_MAX_ITEM,
 				BRCMF_H2D_TXFLOWRING_ITEMSIZE, dma_buf);
+	atomic_set(&msgbuf->flowrings[flowid]->outstanding_tx, 0);
 
 	commonring = msgbuf->commonrings[BRCMF_H2D_MSGRING_CONTROL_SUBMIT];
 	brcmf_commonring_lock(commonring);
@@ -1295,6 +1295,10 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_process_flow_ring_delete_response(struct brcmf_msgbuf *msgbuf,
 	}
 	brcmf_dbg(MSGBUF, "Flowring %d Delete response status %d\n", flowid,
 		  status);
+	if (atomic_read(&msgbuf->flowrings[flowid]->outstanding_tx))
+		brcmf_dbg(MSGBUF, "Flowring %d deleted with %d tx status outstanding\n",
+			  flowid,
+			  atomic_read(&msgbuf->flowrings[flowid]->outstanding_tx));
 
 	brcmf_msgbuf_remove_flowring(msgbuf, flowid);
 }
@@ -1436,23 +1440,16 @@ void brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring(struct brcmf_pub *drvr, u16 flowid)
 	void *ret_ptr;
 	u8 ifidx;
 	int err;
-	int retry = BRCMF_MAX_TXSTATUS_WAIT_RETRIES;
 
-	/* make sure it is not in txflow */
+	/*
+	 * Make sure txflow posts nothing more to the ring. The firmware returns
+	 * the tx status of the posted packets when it deletes the ring, before
+	 * it sends the delete response.
+	 */
 	brcmf_commonring_lock(commonring_del);
 	flow->rings[flowid]->status = RING_CLOSING;
 	brcmf_commonring_unlock(commonring_del);
 
-	/* wait for commonring txflow finished */
-	while (retry && atomic_read(&commonring_del->outstanding_tx)) {
-		usleep_range(5000, 10000);
-		retry--;
-	}
-	if (!retry) {
-		brcmf_err("timed out waiting for txstatus\n");
-		atomic_set(&commonring_del->outstanding_tx, 0);
-	}
-
 	/* no need to submit if firmware can not be reached */
 	if (drvr->bus_if->state != BRCMF_BUS_UP) {
 		brcmf_dbg(MSGBUF, "bus down, flowring will be removed\n");
